    <title>Medications</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Medication</th><th>Frequency</th><th>Route</th><th>Dates</th><th>Status</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr ID="medication-1"><td>Buprenorphine 8 mg and naloxone 2 mg sublingual film: half a film (4 mg) on day 1, then one film (8 mg) under the tongue daily</td><td>One film under the tongue daily after a 4 mg first dose</td><td>Sublingual route</td><td>2026-04-20 to 2026-04-27</td><td>completed</td><td>S</td></tr><tr ID="medication-2"><td>Buprenorphine 8 mg and naloxone 2 mg sublingual film, two films (16 mg) under the tongue once daily</td><td>Two films under the tongue once daily</td><td>Sublingual route</td><td>2026-04-27</td><td>active</td><td>S</td></tr><tr ID="medication-3"><td>Naloxone 4 mg nasal spray, one spray in one nostril for a suspected opioid overdose; may repeat every 2 to 3 minutes in alternating nostrils; call 911</td><td>One spray (4 mg) in one nostril for suspected overdose; repeat every 2 to 3 minutes if there is no response</td><td>Nasal route</td><td>2026-04-20</td><td>active</td><td>S</td></tr><tr ID="medication-4"><td>Acamprosate 333 mg delayed-release oral tablet, two tablets (666 mg) by mouth three times daily</td><td>Two tablets by mouth three times daily</td><td>Oral route</td><td>2026-04-27</td><td>active</td><td>S</td></tr><tr ID="medication-5"><td>Thiamine 100 mg oral tablet, one tablet by mouth daily</td><td>One tablet by mouth daily</td><td>Oral route</td><td>2026-04-20 to 2026-10-19</td><td>completed</td><td>S</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

