    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Opioid use disorder (heroin), severe; in early remission in a controlled environment at intake, five weeks after release from custody; on buprenorphine; synthetic modern episode linked to her documented heroin use</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>F11.20</td><td>S — Synthetic modern coding of the documented heroin addiction; language is person-first, and the code does not change with a return to use.</td>
